WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.173 --> 00:00:09.944
Oh. Riiick...

2
00:00:09.978 --> 00:00:14.114
You were right. Morty.

3
00:00:14.849 --> 00:00:19.019
Chili...was too...spicy.

4
00:00:20.622 --> 00:00:22.557
Ohhh...
Ah.

5
00:00:22.590 --> 00:00:24.324
Oh.

6
00:00:28.095 --> 00:00:31.131
Estate sale is open!

7
00:00:31.164 --> 00:00:33.267
Getcha post-its out.
first come. first serve.

8
00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:34.736
If you see a post-it.

9
00:00:34.769 --> 00:00:36.270
the item has
already been claimed.

10
00:00:36.303 --> 00:00:37.872
- Oh. yeah.
- Alright.

11
00:00:37.906 --> 00:00:39.273
Hey. nice office chair.

12
00:00:39.306 --> 00:00:41.041
Hatchi-Matchi.

13
00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.544
Pretty ghoulish.
don't you think?

14
00:00:42.577 --> 00:00:44.712
W-we just get to
take anything we want?

15
00:00:44.746 --> 00:00:47.015
Morty. they're dead.
You want to be buried
with your porn magazines?

16
00:00:47.047 --> 00:00:48.315
Magazines?

17
00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.250
W-what's a magazines.
old man?

18
00:00:50.284 --> 00:00:52.386
Fuck you. Morty.
Go practice your pronouns.

19
00:00:52.419 --> 00:00:54.321
Whoa!

20
00:00:54.354 --> 00:00:56.925
An in-ground
two-post vehicle lift?

21
00:00:56.958 --> 00:00:58.960
You could park a motorcycle
on this bad boy

22
00:00:58.993 --> 00:01:00.695
and rotate it
any which way.

23
00:01:00.728 --> 00:01:03.263
I put my post-it
on it first.
No. no. I did!

24
00:01:03.297 --> 00:01:04.732
I come from a water planet.

25
00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:06.000
I should get the snorkel.

26
00:01:06.034 --> 00:01:07.067
If you're from
a water planet.

27
00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:08.603
why do you need a snorkel?

28
00:01:12.239 --> 00:01:15.510
These estate sales
are lame af. am I right?

29
00:01:15.543 --> 00:01:16.310
Yeah.

30
00:01:16.343 --> 00:01:17.745
I came to funeral hop.

31
00:01:17.779 --> 00:01:18.846
but there aren't
any Smiths left

32
00:01:18.880 --> 00:01:20.447
to hold a funeral.

33
00:01:20.480 --> 00:01:21.448
Wait. funeral hop?

34
00:01:21.481 --> 00:01:22.584
Oh. shit.

35
00:01:22.617 --> 00:01:23.985
You gotta try it. dude.

36
00:01:24.018 --> 00:01:26.186
Some version of your mom.

37
00:01:26.219 --> 00:01:27.789
your dad.
bawling their eyes out

38
00:01:27.822 --> 00:01:29.991
and saying the <i>nicest</i> shit
you've ever heard.

39
00:01:30.024 --> 00:01:31.491
But -- can't happen when
the whole family

40
00:01:31.526 --> 00:01:33.061
checks out
at the same time.

41
00:01:33.093 --> 00:01:35.195
Your Rick brings you
to your own funerals?

42
00:01:35.228 --> 00:01:37.799
Nah. dawg.
I drive myself.

43
00:01:37.832 --> 00:01:40.167
Whoa.
You don't got a Portal Jr.?

44
00:01:40.200 --> 00:01:41.769
Shit. bunch of us have one.

45
00:01:41.803 --> 00:01:43.671
Let's see. I bet...

46
00:01:44.772 --> 00:01:46.007
Bam.

47
00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.174
Pop a post-it
on that bad boy

48
00:01:47.207 --> 00:01:48.543
before someone else does.

49
00:01:48.576 --> 00:01:49.677
Thanks.

50
00:01:49.711 --> 00:01:51.111
And. uh. c-cool sunglasses.

51
00:01:51.144 --> 00:01:52.914
Sunglasses?

52
00:01:52.947 --> 00:01:53.982
These are my eyes.

53
00:02:03.057 --> 00:02:04.324
Um. Rick.

54
00:02:04.358 --> 00:02:05.927
you ever gone
to your own funeral?

55
00:02:05.960 --> 00:02:07.562
Is that new slang
for taking a dump?

56
00:02:07.595 --> 00:02:08.796
What? No.

57
00:02:08.830 --> 00:02:10.098
Well.
I'm gonna start using it.

58
00:02:10.130 --> 00:02:11.131
Look. a Morty
at the estate sale

59
00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.667
was a funeral hopper. and --

60
00:02:12.700 --> 00:02:14.201
Ugh. you can do better than
getting emotional handjobs

61
00:02:14.234 --> 00:02:15.235
from a fake family.

62
00:02:15.268 --> 00:02:16.871
My real family is dead.

63
00:02:16.904 --> 00:02:18.506
Wow. what a zing.
So is mine.

64
00:02:18.539 --> 00:02:21.009
The only thing that helps
ease the horror of existence

65
00:02:21.042 --> 00:02:22.744
is friction-free rotation.

66
00:02:22.777 --> 00:02:25.980
Did you buy a motorcycle
to justify the platform?

67
00:02:26.014 --> 00:02:27.548
Morty. <i>it turns.</i>

68
00:02:27.582 --> 00:02:29.651
C'mon. man.
I'm asking for guidance.

69
00:02:29.684 --> 00:02:31.986
Do whatever you want.
It's your funeral.

70
00:02:48.335 --> 00:02:49.671
Thank you.

71
00:02:49.704 --> 00:02:53.107
Big Legs Morty
loved Ritchie Valens.

72
00:02:53.141 --> 00:02:55.342
And now
his Big Legs Grandfather

73
00:02:55.375 --> 00:02:56.844
is gonna say a few words.

74
00:02:56.878 --> 00:02:59.346
What!
Let me grieve!

75
00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.882
You've been drunk all week.

76
00:03:00.915 --> 00:03:02.550
<i>Maybe</i> if you had been sober.

77
00:03:02.583 --> 00:03:04.217
you wouldn't have
microwaved him.

78
00:03:04.251 --> 00:03:06.688
His big legs were wet!

79
00:03:06.721 --> 00:03:08.122
I should have guessed.

80
00:03:08.156 --> 00:03:09.624
Wait! Big Legs Morty.

81
00:03:09.657 --> 00:03:12.593
I should have done this
when you were alive.

82
00:03:14.996 --> 00:03:17.031
Oh. hell yeah!

83
00:03:56.804 --> 00:03:59.941
Well. I guess
this is gonna be hard.

84
00:03:59.974 --> 00:04:01.609
but Mort loved
to do hard things.

85
00:04:01.642 --> 00:04:03.978
So...
we're gonna do this for him.

86
00:04:05.479 --> 00:04:08.248
How many of you here
<i>loved</i> my son?

87
00:04:08.281 --> 00:04:10.218
- Yeah...
- Yeah.

88
00:04:10.250 --> 00:04:11.652
<i>I asked...</i>

89
00:04:11.686 --> 00:04:15.089
how many of you here
<i>loved my son?!</i>

90
00:04:18.226 --> 00:04:20.862
Maybe you loved him
because he was a leader.

91
00:04:20.895 --> 00:04:24.132
a scholar. an athlete.

92
00:04:24.165 --> 00:04:27.300
I loved him
because he was <i>mine.</i>

93
00:04:27.334 --> 00:04:29.269
Because he was my son.

94
00:04:29.302 --> 00:04:30.505
We love you. Mort!

95
00:04:30.538 --> 00:04:32.507
Mort! Mort! Mort! Mort!

96
00:04:32.540 --> 00:04:38.246
When I die. I will
kill God for taking my boy!

97
00:04:38.278 --> 00:04:41.115
I don't approve of
your promise.

98
00:04:41.149 --> 00:04:42.382
but I understand.

99
00:04:44.852 --> 00:04:48.022
Who will be there for me
now that you're gone?

100
00:04:50.390 --> 00:04:52.026
Chesterfield?

101
00:04:52.059 --> 00:04:53.393
Oh. oh!
No. no. no. no. no. no!

102
00:04:53.426 --> 00:04:55.830
Oh!
Stop. stop!

103
00:04:55.863 --> 00:04:57.397
Mort?

104
00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:59.934
Oh...no...

105
00:04:59.967 --> 00:05:02.435
You guys have never
seen another Morty before?

106
00:05:02.469 --> 00:05:03.938
Oh!

107
00:05:03.971 --> 00:05:05.405
Oh!

108
00:05:05.438 --> 00:05:07.008
Does that make sense?

109
00:05:07.041 --> 00:05:10.845
S-shortest version is --
infinite me's. infinite you's.

110
00:05:10.878 --> 00:05:12.013
You want a grilled cheese?

111
00:05:12.046 --> 00:05:13.380
I want to make it for him.

112
00:05:13.413 --> 00:05:14.481
And this thing?

113
00:05:14.515 --> 00:05:15.716
It's how I got here.

114
00:05:15.750 --> 00:05:16.751
Rick made it for me.

115
00:05:16.784 --> 00:05:20.021
Not my Rick --
i-it's a lot of canon.

116
00:05:20.054 --> 00:05:21.522
Where is Rick?

117
00:05:21.556 --> 00:05:22.990
I'm sorry to tell you this.

118
00:05:23.024 --> 00:05:24.759
but. um...

119
00:05:24.792 --> 00:05:26.294
...our Rick...

120
00:05:26.326 --> 00:05:28.930
...is a drunk. Morty.

121
00:05:28.963 --> 00:05:31.566
Ohh...No?

122
00:05:31.599 --> 00:05:33.466
We had to end our
relationship with him.

123
00:05:33.501 --> 00:05:34.869
We tried everything to help.

124
00:05:34.902 --> 00:05:36.604
but ultimately.
he needed to help himself.

125
00:05:36.637 --> 00:05:38.506
And he. like. listened?

126
00:05:38.539 --> 00:05:40.208
This universe <i>is</i> wild.

127
00:05:40.241 --> 00:05:41.509
Just the way you like it.

128
00:05:41.542 --> 00:05:43.077
Mmm.

129
00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:44.879
Wow. So good.

130
00:05:44.912 --> 00:05:46.881
Don't suppose
there's any tomato soup --

131
00:05:46.914 --> 00:05:47.982
Holy shit.

132
00:05:48.015 --> 00:05:49.382
You guys are something else.

133
00:05:49.416 --> 00:05:50.885
You should have met our Mort.

134
00:05:51.686 --> 00:05:53.721
<i>Ray.</i>
<i>like it or not...</i>

135
00:05:53.754 --> 00:05:55.957
Mm.
<i>...the bank's gonna</i>
<i>take your farm.</i>

136
00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:57.792
<i>They will come. Ray.</i>

137
00:05:57.825 --> 00:05:59.227
Huh?
Oh. my gosh.

138
00:05:59.260 --> 00:06:01.162
My family's probably worried.

139
00:06:01.195 --> 00:06:03.564
My...other family.
You're leaving?

140
00:06:03.598 --> 00:06:05.465
Summer.
he's not ours to keep.

141
00:06:05.498 --> 00:06:06.968
I understand. Mort --

142
00:06:07.001 --> 00:06:08.569
I mean. Morty.

143
00:06:10.171 --> 00:06:11.572
Come back to us. kiddo.

144
00:06:11.606 --> 00:06:13.941
Whenever you want.
you come back.

145
00:06:17.945 --> 00:06:20.715
Summer.
stop live-streaming!

146
00:06:26.053 --> 00:06:27.487
Where have you been?

147
00:06:27.521 --> 00:06:29.123
I've needed you to hand me
wrenches and stuff.

148
00:06:29.156 --> 00:06:30.892
Check this out.

149
00:06:30.925 --> 00:06:32.126
Wow. great.

150
00:06:32.159 --> 00:06:34.128
Huh? Ah!
Oh. Rick!

151
00:06:34.161 --> 00:06:35.495
It's pulling my insides!

152
00:06:35.529 --> 00:06:37.098
You have too much
metal in you dipshit.

153
00:06:37.131 --> 00:06:38.566
Oh!

154
00:06:38.599 --> 00:06:40.701
I didn't put it there.
So?

155
00:06:49.777 --> 00:06:51.045
Oh. hey!
Hey!

156
00:06:51.078 --> 00:06:52.613
Morty. you came back!

157
00:06:52.647 --> 00:06:54.515
Oh. geez. G-Good boy.

158
00:06:54.548 --> 00:06:56.483
That's a dog for ya.

159
00:06:56.517 --> 00:06:58.185
M-my dog enslaved me.

160
00:06:58.219 --> 00:06:59.587
B-but not this one.

161
00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:01.155
So I'm hanging out
of the side

162
00:07:01.188 --> 00:07:02.390
of the ship in space.

163
00:07:02.422 --> 00:07:03.925
holding the guitar
that Rick wanted.

164
00:07:03.958 --> 00:07:05.593
but my eyes burst from
the pressure difference

165
00:07:05.626 --> 00:07:07.395
and I couldn't see
for. like. an hour.

166
00:07:07.427 --> 00:07:09.397
Morty.
you could have been killed.

167
00:07:09.429 --> 00:07:11.866
Oh. yeah. I was.

168
00:07:11.899 --> 00:07:13.000
You <i>died?</i>

169
00:07:13.034 --> 00:07:14.602
You die. and come back?

170
00:07:14.635 --> 00:07:16.404
The worst part
is waking up in the tube.

171
00:07:16.436 --> 00:07:18.172
where the fresh body is

172
00:07:18.205 --> 00:07:20.608
c-cause you have to cough all
that fluid out of your lungs.

173
00:07:20.641 --> 00:07:22.743
You're saying
where you come from.

174
00:07:22.777 --> 00:07:27.248
your grandfather lets you die
over and over again?

175
00:07:27.281 --> 00:07:29.383
What does your father
say about this?

176
00:07:29.417 --> 00:07:31.552
♪ Who's a Mad Men? ♪

177
00:07:31.585 --> 00:07:33.854
♪ I'm a Mad Men ♪

178
00:07:37.591 --> 00:07:40.094
Oh. my God.
I <i>made</i> an owl.

179
00:07:40.127 --> 00:07:41.461
T-this is incredible.

180
00:07:41.494 --> 00:07:43.698
Too bad my big lathe
is up at the cabin.

181
00:07:43.731 --> 00:07:45.533
Built it with my dad.

182
00:07:45.566 --> 00:07:46.901
Then Mort helped me put up

183
00:07:46.934 --> 00:07:48.602
the sleeping porch
just last summer.

184
00:07:48.636 --> 00:07:50.638
Wish we could take you
there this weekend.

185
00:07:50.671 --> 00:07:52.573
but the gals are going to be
at the soup kitchen and...

186
00:07:52.606 --> 00:07:55.042
I mean.
<i>we</i> could head up there.

187
00:07:55.076 --> 00:07:56.310
just the two of us?

188
00:07:56.344 --> 00:07:58.612
Really?
You'd want to do that?

189
00:08:07.688 --> 00:08:09.223
Don't you have any matches?

190
00:08:09.256 --> 00:08:10.825
A man who relies on matches

191
00:08:10.858 --> 00:08:12.827
gets pretty cold
when he runs out.

192
00:08:14.494 --> 00:08:16.063
You feel like a steak?

193
00:08:18.532 --> 00:08:21.202
Wait till the pan
releases the meat.

194
00:08:26.073 --> 00:08:29.977
I feel like I've never
learned anything until now.

195
00:08:31.278 --> 00:08:34.482
...And Mort.
he's climbing so fast.

196
00:08:34.515 --> 00:08:35.816
When he loses his footing.

197
00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:38.019
he's just silent
as he falls...

198
00:08:38.052 --> 00:08:40.521
...until the crack
of his body hitting stone.

199
00:08:42.423 --> 00:08:44.025
Mort was so strong.

200
00:08:44.058 --> 00:08:46.293
but I wasn't strong enough
to save him.

201
00:08:46.327 --> 00:08:48.629
I'm so sorry.

202
00:08:48.662 --> 00:08:50.631
I know you're not my Mort...

203
00:08:50.664 --> 00:08:53.234
Not really...

204
00:08:53.267 --> 00:08:55.403
...but I love you
just the same.

205
00:08:56.537 --> 00:08:58.105
I-I love you. dad.

206
00:08:58.139 --> 00:09:00.141
I-I want to be your son.

207
00:09:00.174 --> 00:09:02.276
I <i>am</i> your son.

208
00:09:06.447 --> 00:09:08.482
Then break the gun.

209
00:09:08.517 --> 00:09:11.018
What?
This isn't one of
your adventures.

210
00:09:11.052 --> 00:09:12.787
It can be your life.

211
00:09:12.820 --> 00:09:14.355
But what if I need to --

212
00:09:14.388 --> 00:09:15.756
What could you need
that isn't here?

213
00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:17.591
A family that
doesn't appreciate you?

214
00:09:17.625 --> 00:09:19.693
A resurrection machine that
makes infinite grandpas?

215
00:09:19.727 --> 00:09:22.296
You need to turn into
a fucking giraffe?

216
00:09:22.329 --> 00:09:23.964
Do it!

217
00:09:23.998 --> 00:09:25.299
Uh...

218
00:09:25.332 --> 00:09:26.567
Hey!

219
00:09:27.802 --> 00:09:29.370
Oh. my God!

220
00:09:29.403 --> 00:09:31.772
Yes! I love you!

221
00:09:31.806 --> 00:09:34.543
I tried to make my son strong.

222
00:09:34.575 --> 00:09:36.777
So strong he would never die!

223
00:09:36.811 --> 00:09:38.813
Ah!

224
00:09:46.320 --> 00:09:48.956
I just want to keep you safe!

225
00:09:48.989 --> 00:09:50.458
Mort?

226
00:09:50.491 --> 00:09:51.892
Mort.

227
00:09:51.926 --> 00:09:53.227
Mort?

228
00:09:54.161 --> 00:09:55.729
Mort!

229
00:09:55.763 --> 00:09:57.498
Come back.

230
00:10:02.269 --> 00:10:05.106
<i>Dad wants me</i>
<i>to free solo El Capitan.</i>

231
00:10:05.139 --> 00:10:06.707
<i>He's crazy.</i>

232
00:10:06.740 --> 00:10:08.543
<i>He wants me to be able</i>
<i>to survive anything.</i>

233
00:10:08.577 --> 00:10:10.177
<i>My only hope's to run away.</i>

234
00:10:10.744 --> 00:10:12.346
Thank you. Mort.

235
00:10:44.812 --> 00:10:47.047
...And we're left with
a radical non-duality.

236
00:10:47.081 --> 00:10:49.450
The universe is
not locally real.

237
00:10:49.483 --> 00:10:51.952
Which means nothing matters...

238
00:10:51.986 --> 00:10:55.122
...or <i>everything</i> does.

239
00:10:56.223 --> 00:10:58.125
Moral universe. let's go!

240
00:10:59.493 --> 00:11:00.595
I fucking knew it.

241
00:11:00.629 --> 00:11:01.862
The Central Finite Curve.

242
00:11:01.896 --> 00:11:03.364
portal travel.
all of it.

243
00:11:03.397 --> 00:11:04.965
Of course there's
infinite Mortys --

244
00:11:04.999 --> 00:11:07.234
because there's
infinite worlds. Morty.

245
00:11:07.268 --> 00:11:08.869
<i>and</i> infinite me's!

246
00:11:08.903 --> 00:11:10.704
A-am I cool in most worlds?

247
00:11:10.738 --> 00:11:12.641
Oh!
Mr. Sanchez?

248
00:11:12.673 --> 00:11:14.742
Oh. sorry I frighten you.

249
00:11:14.775 --> 00:11:16.277
I am from Russia.

250
00:11:16.977 --> 00:11:18.779
Who is hunting you?

251
00:11:18.812 --> 00:11:20.848
Jerry? I don't know.
Ma-maybe all of them?

252
00:11:20.881 --> 00:11:22.183
I just want to go home.

253
00:11:22.216 --> 00:11:23.684
I thought there
was a better version

254
00:11:23.717 --> 00:11:26.120
of my family for me.
but I was wrong.

255
00:11:26.153 --> 00:11:27.888
Do you think
you could make this?

256
00:11:27.922 --> 00:11:30.157
Oh. Morty.
I would love to help you.

257
00:11:30.191 --> 00:11:32.760
but that thing
almost destroyed me.

258
00:11:32.793 --> 00:11:35.296
Salieri to infinite Mozarts.

259
00:11:36.063 --> 00:11:37.932
Do -- Do you guys
not have Mozart?

260
00:11:37.965 --> 00:11:40.434
Oh. Morty.
we gotta watch "Amadeus."

261
00:11:40.467 --> 00:11:41.735
Shit. I'm late.

262
00:11:41.769 --> 00:11:42.937
